exercises.question:
Create a new Java program by creating a folder "src" and a folder "out", and create a new file "Calculator.java" in the "src" directory. Insert the following source code into the file using a text editor of your choice. Compile the program so that the compiled output is placed in the "out" directory, run the file, and commit the new source file to the Git repository.

public class Calculator {
public int add(int a, int b) {
return a + b;
}
public int subtract(int a, int b) {
return a - b;
}
public int multiply(int a, int b) {
return a + b;
}
public int divide(int a, int b) {
if (b == 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Division by zero");
return a / b;
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
Calculator calculator = new Calculator();
System.out.println("Add: 5+3=" + calculator.add(5, 3));
System.out.println("Subtract: 5-3=" + calculator.subtract(5, 3));
System.out.println("Multiply: 5*3=" + calculator.multiply(5, 3));
System.out.println("Divide: 5/3=" + calculator.divide(5, 3));
}
}

Create a new feature branch "feature/advanced-math" to extend the program and switch to this branch. Add the following additional methods after the "divide" method in the Calculator class and commit the changes.

public int modulus(int a, int b) {
return a % b;
}
public int square(int a) {
return a * a;
}

Switch back to the "main" branch. Then create a second branch "feature/pi", add the following method also after the "divide" method of the Calculator class, and commit the changes:

public static double getPi() {
return Math.PI;
}

exercises.correct_answer:
# From feature/pi back to main (if not already there)
git checkout main
# Merge first feature branch (no conflict expected)
git merge feature/advanced-math
# Merge second feature branch - this triggers a conflict
(same insertion point)
git merge feature/pi
# => Git reports merge conflict in src/Calculator.java
# Open file and manually resolve conflict markers >>>>>>
nano src/Calculator.java
# After resolving: File with ALL three new methods
(modulus, square, getPi)
git add src/Calculator.java
git commit -m "Resolve merge conflict: combine advanced-math and pi methods"

Example of a resolved final version (src/Calculator.java):
public class Calculator {
public int add(int a, int b) {
return a + b;
}
public int subtract(int a, int b) {
return a - b;
}
public int multiply(int a, int b) {
return a + b; // intentional error for later tests
}
public int divide(int a, int b) {
if (b == 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Division by zero");
return a / b;
}
// Additions from feature/advanced-math
public int modulus(int a, int b) {
return a % b;
}
public int square(int a) {
return a * a;
}
// Addition from feature/pi
public static double getPi() {
return Math.PI;
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
Calculator calculator = new Calculator();
System.out.println("Add: 5+3=" + calculator.add(5, 3));
System.out.println("Subtract: 5-3=" + calculator.subtract(5, 3));
System.out.println("Multiply: 5*3=" + calculator.multiply(5, 3));
System.out.println("Divide: 5/3=" + calculator.divide(5, 3));
System.out.println("Modulus: 5%3=" + calculator.modulus(5, 3));
System.out.println("Square: 5^2=" + calculator.square(5));
System.out.println("Pi=" + Calculator.getPi());
}
}

